[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=1Password
Exec=/opt/1Password/1password --silent
Hidden=true
NotShowIn=XFCE;GNOME;KDE;
X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=false
Comment=Autostart DISABLED by vps-info. 1Password lifecycle is owned by 1password-desktop.service (RuntimeMaxSec=2h), started on demand by x11vnc -afteraccept. XFCE autostart bypassed that cap and spawned a throwaway instance on every VNC connect. File is chattr +i so 1Password cannot rewrite it; to re-enable: sudo chattr -i this file.
